# Vendor Assignments Portal — repository hygiene
#
# This repo is public and the site is served from its root, so anything committed
# here is published. It has no build step and no dependencies; these patterns
# exist so that a stray install or a scratch file cannot end up deployed.

# ---- dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
# The app has none. A local `npm install` to run a one-off script writes these.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
npm-shrinkwrap.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
npm-debug.log*

# ---- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# config.js IS committed on purpose: it holds only the Supabase anon key, which
# is public by design — row-level security is the boundary, not key secrecy, and
# the sibling apps commit the same value. A service-role key must never be, so
# anything shaped like one stays out.
*service_role*
*.secret
.env
.env.*
secrets.json

# ---- scratch ----------------------------------------------------------------
*.local.*
*_scratch.*
scratch/
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ---- source workbooks -------------------------------------------------------
# The RE2 export and the division starts logs are business data and are not small.
# They are uploaded through the app, never committed.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls

# ---- editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
